title: mf script new
tags: [[CLI command]] [[Scripting the GUI]]
kind: reference
summary: Copy a template into the scripts directory, to adapt it (asks which one when none is named, on a terminal)

`mf script new [TEMPLATE] [--name NAME]` copies a template from
`~/.config/metafolder/scripts/templates/` into `~/.config/metafolder/scripts/` and
prints the new file's path, ready to edit. The template is named with or without
`.sh`; the copy keeps its name unless `--name` gives another.

* Without a template, on a terminal, it lists them, numbered, and asks which one — a number or a name. Not on a terminal (a script, a pipe), that is a usage error naming them (exit 2).
* It never overwrites: a script of that name already there is an error (exit 1), the file left untouched.

The copy is an ordinary file of the configuration: `metafolder-sync-config` keeps it,
and a later version of the template does not change it ([[Updating the configuration]]).
